WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.250
Just because an actor is contracted to film
a movie, that doesn't mean they're forced

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:06.560
to do every scene in the original script.

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:11.060
From nudes to feuds, here's a look at movie
scenes that actors refused to film.

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:16.750
As super-spy Eggsy in the Kingsman series,
Taron Egerton has skyrocketed from a relative

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:18.860
unknown to an in-demand leading man.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:23.779
Despite his worldwide success, a steamy scene
with Poppy Delevingne in the second installment

00:00:23.779 --> 00:00:28.650
of the spy franchise, Kingsman: The Golden
Circle, was a little too hot for him to handle.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:34.079
In the scene, Egerton's Eggsy is under pressure
to place a tracking device, uh, inside Delevingne's

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:35.880
Clara during an intimate moment.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:39.680
However, Egerton was incredibly uncomfortable
with the planned scene.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:41.240
"I'm sorry, I can't.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:42.800
I'm in a relationship."

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:44.020
"That's adorable."

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.660
Instead, Delevingne's real-life husband played
Eggsy's hand in the shot.

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:52.049
Egerton himself seemed relieved, later saying,
"He saved the world."

00:00:53.069 --> 00:00:58.160
Back in 2008, Four Christmases sounded like
the best idea since Christmas tree cakes and

00:00:58.160 --> 00:00:59.300
rum-spiked eggnog.

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:03.680
Put America's sweetheart Reese Witherspoon
and funnyman Vince Vaughn together as a couple

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:07.630
that's forced to spend Christmas with their
disapproving, divorced relatives and holiday

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:08.760
chaos ensues.

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:13.060
However, the reviews were abysmal, with many
critics panning the lack of chemistry between

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:13.560
the leads.

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:18.060
As it turns out, it was a Christmas miracle
the film got finished at all, since Witherspoon

00:01:18.079 --> 00:01:20.150
and Vaughn couldn't stand each other.

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:24.500
The two were complete opposites from the beginning:
She arrived bright and early to the set; he

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:27.020
would wander in looking like he partied the
night before.

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:30.100
She wanted to rehearse and block scenes; he
wanted to ad-lib.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:34.310
Their relationship grew so cold that Reese
is reported to have refused a bedroom scene

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:37.390
with Vaughn which was ultimately scrapped
from the finished film.

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:40.700
It sounds like there could've been a better
way for the two co-stars to get along.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:43.210
"Even Santa Claus don't love me!"

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:45.720
"Hey, that's not gonna bring back Santa, that's
not gonna bring-"

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:50.040
"When he gets to hurting inside and can't
use his emotion words, he takes to streaking."

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:54.939
If you've ever seen Borat, Bruno, or basically
any of Sacha Baron Cohen's work, you know

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:58.100
the dude has zero issues with filming in his
birthday suit.

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:03.260
So it's no surprise that he expects the same
nonchalance about nudity from his co-stars.

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:08.390
However, one of his famous female scene partners
flat-out refused to go nude, despite Cohen's

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:08.880
badgering.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:12.840
Rebel Wilson is known for her bawdy, anything-goes
brand of humor.

00:02:12.849 --> 00:02:16.799
However, she refuses to go nude and it is
written into her contract that her clothes

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:17.380
stay on.

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:22.380
In 2016's The Brothers Grimsby, Wilson played
the girlfriend of Cohen's screw-up turned

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:27.220
spy character, and one scene called for full-frontal
nudity, against her wishes.

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:30.069
Wilson won the battle, not that many people
would know.

00:02:30.069 --> 00:02:34.980
The Brothers Grimsby earned an atrocious $25
million total at the worldwide box office,

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:37.280
or less than what Borat made in one weekend.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:42.860
Amber Heard has gone nude on film before,
but when it came time to go topless for 2018's

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:48.980
London Fields, she flat-out refused, and consequently
was sued by producers for $10 million.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:54.040
Based on the novel of the same name, the film
stars Heard as Nicola Six, a clairvoyant femme

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:57.239
fatale who predicts she'll be murdered by
one of her three lovers.

00:02:57.239 --> 00:03:01.431
Given both the script and the novel it was
based on contained nude scenes, producers

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:04.280
argued that Heard was well aware she'd be
asked to go nude.

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:08.560
Producers argued that her unwillingness to
strip for the film severely disrupted the

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:12.959
production and that she tried to pull the
film from the Toronto International Film Festival

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:14.799
lineup in 2015.

00:03:14.799 --> 00:03:20.560
The production company, Nicola Six Limited,
sued Heard for $10 million, or about 40 times

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:24.959
what London Fields eventually made at the
domestic box office when it was finally released

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:26.020
in 2018.

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:30.500
Its $250,000 take makes it one of the biggest
bombs in history.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:36.050
The 1994 romantic comedy I Love Trouble is
most remembered these days for inspiring one

00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:38.690
of the most notorious co-star feuds ever.

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:43.879
Julia Roberts and Nick Nolte star as dueling
Chicago reporters chasing the same scoop.

00:03:43.879 --> 00:03:48.849
Murder, mayhem and romance ensue, and while
the filmmakers were hoping for a Tracy-Hepburn

00:03:48.849 --> 00:03:52.300
spark, what they got was a Nolte-Roberts dumpster
fire.

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:56.620
"Peterson!"

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:57.640
"Self-defense classes.

00:03:58.140 --> 00:03:59.420
A must for a woman in the 90s."

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:04.720
Supposedly, Roberts disliked Nolte's loutish
machismo so much that she would insult him

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:05.420
on set.

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:09.100
Nolte grew so tired of this that he'd act
up just to spite her.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:14.180
It got so bad the two refused to film their
scenes together and acted with stand-ins instead.

00:04:14.409 --> 00:04:19.060
Roberts and Nolte played nice during promotion,
but proving that time does not heal all wounds,

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:21.340
they continued to hold a grudge years later.

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:25.520
In 2003, Roberts called Nolte a "disgusting"
human being.

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:26.560
Nolte responded:

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:28.830
"It's not nice to call someone 'disgusting.'

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:30.140
But she's not a nice person.

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:31.240
Everyone knows that."

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:36.130
Nick Nolte has been nominated for an Academy
Award three times, while Julia Roberts won

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:38.060
one for 2000's Erin Brockovich.

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:42.260
Sounds like both of them deserved an Oscar
for even briefly pretending to like each other.

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:47.420
Jim Caviezel became a household name, if not
a Hollywood A-lister, for his role as Jesus

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:51.980
Christ in Mel Gibson's 2003 passion project
The Passion of the Christ.

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:56.180
Before going Biblical, Caviezel was well on
his way to being the next big blockbuster

00:04:56.190 --> 00:05:01.300
heartthrob with parts in Frequency, The Count
of Monte Cristo, and Angel Eyes.

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:06.250
It was in the latter two that the devout Catholic
earned himself a reputation for refusing explicit

00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:07.000
sex scenes.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:11.540
Tinseltown is a tough place for chastity,
and Caviezel raised eyebrows when he would

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:15.880
only do a love scene with Jennifer Lopez in
Angel Eyes if she kept her clothes on.

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:20.950
He likewise refused to film a scene with his
Monte Cristo co-star Dagmara Domińczyk unless

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:22.360
she put something between them.

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:26.690
Caviezel has argued that his commitment to
staying clothed is out of respect for his

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:28.140
wife and his Catholic faith:

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:32.120
"If it is embarrassing for people on set,
if they think you're a wimp, that you're an

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:36.000
embarrassment, talking this way, well, I'd
rather be embarrassed before the whole country

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:36.840
than before God."

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:42.720
Will Smith was riding high in the early 1990s
with a successful hip-hop career and an even

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:45.800
more successful TV show, The Fresh Prince
of Bel Air.

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:50.171
Before discovering his penchant for making
broadly appealing blockbuster movies, Smith

00:05:50.171 --> 00:05:55.740
sought to establish himself as serious actor
right out of the gate with 1993's Six Degrees

00:05:55.740 --> 00:05:56.720
of Separation.

00:05:56.760 --> 00:06:01.820
Based on the play of the same name, the movie
has a dense, character-driven plot and complicated

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:05.740
themes, and while Smith was willing to take
a risk, the script called for something he

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:06.640
refused to do.

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:12.050
In the film, Smith's gay character is required
to share a passionate kiss with his male co-star,

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:13.220
Anthony Michael Hall.

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:17.640
Smith was uncomfortable with this and sought
advice from Denzel Washington, who supposedly

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:19.680
told him not to kiss a man on camera.

00:06:19.910 --> 00:06:24.240
So that's precisely what Smith didn't do:
The shot was filmed from behind, allowing

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:25.320
Smith to fake it.

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:38.960
In the horror spoof sequel Scary Movie 5,
Lindsay Lohan was supposed to kiss Charlie

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:41.460
Sheen three times in their bedroom scene.

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:47.190
However, Lohan refused to lock lips with Sheen
out of fear of germs, or worse, from his hard-partying

00:06:47.190 --> 00:06:47.680
past.

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:52.240
Both stars had already signed releases saying
that they didn't have cold sores, but even

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:56.260
with contractual assurances, Lohan still refused
to smooch.

00:06:56.260 --> 00:07:00.700
While filmmakers tried to use a body double,
they ultimately just dropped most of the kissing

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:01.920
from the scene entirely.

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:02.700
"Ow!"

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:05.460
"Sorry, it's my sobriety monitor.

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:08.840
Charlie, I'm scared."

00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:11.340
"Lindsay, sweetie, there's nothing to be afraid
of."

00:07:11.350 --> 00:07:15.410
Although the pair would eventually lock lips
years later on an episode of Sheen's Anger

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:16.720
Management TV show.

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:21.720
If you think of Wayne's World, you probably
think of Wayne, Garth and the gang head-banging

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:24.600
and lip-synching to Queen's "Bohemian Rhapsody,"
right?

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:29.340
According to Myers, it almost wasn't Queen's
masterpiece they sang to, but a Guns N' Roses

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:32.100
tune, courtesy of director Penelope Spheeris.

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:36.540
She believed that a modern-day rock hit would
fit the bill better than Queen, and Myers

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:38.360
was like “NOT!”

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:43.260
Fortunately, he stuck to his guns and refused
to film the scene unless it was "Bohemian

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:43.760
Rhapsody."

00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:48.940
Despite being his first movie, Myers got his
way, saving the now iconic scene and propelling

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:53.120
Bohemian Rhapsody back up to the Top 40 list
for the first time in years.

